<!--
  The Apple CarPlay mark, without its rounded-square container: the C with the
  play triangle inside it.

  Path taken verbatim from Wikimedia Commons `Apple CarPlay Logo.svg`, which is
  tagged PD-ineligible — the shape is held to be too simple to carry copyright.
  Apple's trademark still applies; labelling the key that launches CarPlay with
  the CarPlay mark is exactly the nominative use that permits.

  Simple Icons, the usual source for monochrome brand glyphs, does not carry
  CarPlay — Apple's marks have been withdrawn from that set — which is why this
  one comes from elsewhere.

  Three things done to the source, all mechanical:

   - The container square is dropped, as asked. It was the only stroked element,
     so what remains is pure fill.
   - The source layers a stroked open arc over the filled band that draws the
     same C. Only the filled band is kept; the two are redundant, and doubling
     them thickens the glyph.
   - VectorDrawable viewports always start at the origin, so the group translates
     the glyph back from the source's offset viewBox. The viewport is then sized
     so the C occupies 80% of it, which is roughly where the design's own key
     icons sit inside their 24-unit box — a circle at the same bounding size
     reads larger than the line glyphs beside it, so it is given a little more
     margin than the Android Auto mark.

  The C's bounds are a circle of radius 44.707 about (85.225, 85.256), i.e.
  x 40.518..129.932, y 40.549..129.963 — 89.414 across. At 80% that needs a
  111.77 box with 11.18 of margin on each side.
-->
